natory text; when you decide to call the tool, emit the tool call itself.\nIf you use MOUSE, include integer row and col arguments.", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "THINKING", "content": "The blue block moved from cols 12-31 to cols 0-19 (far left). The level didn't complete.\nI've been exploring for 106 steps and haven't completed the level. Let me try a completely different approach.\nWhat if the goal is NOT about moving the blue block at all? What if the goal is about the relationship between the charcoal, magenta, and yellow blocks?\nLet me look at the colors more carefully:\n- Charcoal (c): rows 1-3, cols 36-39 (3x4 = 12 pixels)\n- Magenta (M): rows 4-7, cols 36-39 (4x4 = 16 pixels)\n- Yellow (Y): rows 52-59, cols 40-51 (irregular shape, 80 pixels)\n- Blue (b): rows 12-15, cols 0-19 (4x20 = 80 pixels)\nWait, the blue block has 80 pixels, and the yellow shape also has 80 pixels. They have the same pixel count!\nWhat if the goal is to move the blue block to a position where it \"matches\" the yellow shape in some way? But the blue block is a rectangle, and the yellow shape is an irregular shape with a notch. They don't match in shape.\nBut what if the goal is to move the blue block to a position where it has the same pixel count as the yellow shape? The blue block always has 80 pixels, regardless of position. So that doesn't make sense.\nHmm, let me think about this differently. What if the goal is to move the blue block to a position where it \"overlaps\" with the yellow shape when projected vertically? The yellow shape is at rows 52-59, cols 40-51. The blue block is at rows 12-15, cols 0-19. They don't overlap horizontally.\nBut if I move the blue block to cols 40-59, it would overlap horizontally with the yellow shape (cols 40-51). Let me try that.\nFrom the current position (cols 0-19), I need to move RIGHT 10 steps (40 cols) to reach cols 40-59. But the timer might not allow 10 actions.\nActually, let me first reset the level and then move th